#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, liveness]
# doc: |
#   Static use-after-move across a branch join (verdict = elaborate ∘ eval). `s` is
#   moved into `consume(!s)` in ONE arm of an if-without-else, so after the join the
#   place is moved-in-any; the later `print(s)` is a use-after-move. The
#   flow-sensitive liveness gate takes the UNION of the arms (the elab∘eval win) and
#   rejects BEFORE eval with E_UseAfterMove — stdout stays EXACTLY empty (the program
#   never ran, which IS the verdict), exit 1. Sibling of reject_use_after_move.gg on
#   the branch-join axis; flipping the expected `reject:` code must make every lane
#   MISMATCH (Core #6/#8).
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_UseAfterMove
#!end

void consume(String !s):
    pass

void main():
    String s = "hello"
    bool flag = true
    if flag:
        consume(!s)
    print(s)
